{
 "id": "087-dedemin-resim-sergisi",
 "lang": "en",
 "title": "Grandma's Art Show",
 "theme": "Respect for works of art and the artist; expressing feelings about a work",
 "blurb": "Zeynep's grandma hangs her paintings in the living room and opens an exhibition at home; the first visitor is Zeynep. Noticing that her grandma feels shy, Zeynep looks at the paintings slowly; she finds out which were painted from life and which from imagination, and says how each painting makes her feel, and why.",
 "voiceNames": {
  "zeynep": "Zeynep",
  "nine": "Grandma (Zeynep's grandma, the painter)",
  "karamel": "Caramel (cat)"
 },
 "pages": [
  {
   "text": "Zeynep's grandma loves painting. Today she hung her paintings on the living-room wall. One, two, three! “I've opened an exhibition at home,” she said. “You be my first visitor, Zeynep!” Caramel the cat purred: purrr.",
   "hits": {
    "nine": {
     "say": "Welcome, my first visitor!"
    },
    "zeynep": {
     "say": "Hooray, an exhibition at home!"
    },
    "karamel": {
     "say": "Purrr… purrr…"
    }
   },
   "mech": {
    "done": "One, two, three! Grandma's exhibition is ready.",
    "msg": "You counted the paintings!"
   },
   "hint": "Count Grandma's paintings!",
   "ask": "Have you ever been to an exhibition? What did you see there?"
  },
  {
   "text": "Zeynep was still clapping: clap clap clap! But Grandma suddenly went quiet. Her cheeks went red, she rubbed her fingers. “What if you don't like my paintings?” she said softly. Zeynep looked at her carefully. Grandma felt a little shy.",
   "hits": {
    "nine": {
     "say": "What if you don't like my paintings?"
    },
    "zeynep": {
     "say": "Why did Grandma suddenly go quiet?"
    },
    "karamel": {
     "say": "Purrr?"
    }
   },
   "hint": "Touch Grandma!",
   "ask": "How is Grandma feeling? How can you tell?",
   "cues": [
    {
     "w": 3,
     "fx": "alkis"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Zeynep held her grandma's hand. “I'll look at your paintings slowly, slowly,” she said. Caramel reached a paw out to a painting. “Caramel, we look at paintings with our eyes!” said Zeynep. Caramel opened his eyes wide. Grandma smiled. Zeynep wondered: how had Grandma made these paintings?",
   "hits": {
    "nine": {
     "say": "How nicely you look, my dear."
    },
    "zeynep": {
     "say": "I'll look slowly, slowly."
    },
    "karamel": {
     "say": "Meow! I'm looking with my eyes!"
    }
   },
   "predict": {
    "q": "How do you think Grandma made her paintings?",
    "res": "Both are right! A painter looks, and imagines too.",
    "opts": [
     {
      "l": "By looking at things at home"
     },
     {
      "l": "By imagining"
     }
    ]
   },
   "hint": "Touch Zeynep!",
   "ask": "How do we look at a painting? What do you look at when you paint?"
  },
  {
   "text": "Zeynep looked at each painting. The first had a sun and flowers. Oh, the flowers in the pot! The last one had a family holding hands. Oh, that's us! “And the house in the middle?” Grandma winked: “That one I imagined.”",
   "hits": {
    "nine": {
     "say": "Some by looking, some by imagining!"
    },
    "zeynep": {
     "say": "We're in this painting!"
    },
    "r2": {
     "say": "I drew this house from my imagination."
    }
   },
   "mech": {
    "done": "The flowers and we are both in the paintings!",
    "msg": "You found it, the very same!"
   },
   "hint": "Find the painting of the flowers!",
   "ask": "How did Grandma make the painting of the flowers? What would you like to look at while painting?"
  },
  {
   "text": "Zeynep stood in front of each painting. The sunny painting made her cheerful. “Because it's warm!” The house painting made her calm. “Because it's peaceful.” The last painting warmed her heart. “Because it's us!” Grandma listened, listened.",
   "hits": {
    "r1": {
     "say": "It made me cheerful, because it's warm!"
    },
    "r2": {
     "say": "It made me calm, because it's peaceful."
    },
    "r3": {
     "say": "It warmed my heart, because it's us!"
    },
    "nine": {
     "say": "It's lovely to listen to you."
    },
    "zeynep": {
     "say": "Every painting tells me something different."
    },
    "karamel": {
     "say": "Purrr, purrr."
    }
   },
   "hint": "Touch the paintings!",
   "ask": "How did each of these paintings make you feel? Why?"
  },
  {
   "text": "Grandma's eyes sparkled. “You looked at my paintings so nicely,” she said. “And you listened to me.” Then she handed Zeynep the palette. “The next exhibition is yours!” Caramel purred: purrr. Now there were two painters in the living room.",
   "hits": {
    "nine": {
     "say": "The next exhibition is yours!"
    },
    "zeynep": {
     "say": "My first painting will be Caramel!"
    },
    "karamel": {
     "say": "Purrr! Meow!"
    }
   },
   "hint": "Touch Zeynep!",
   "ask": "If you opened an exhibition, what would you hang up? Who would be your first visitor?"
  }
